#### 4.3.4 \(j_{t}\) measurements

From di-hadron correlation function we are able to extract various parameters like width, yield, \(\sqrt{\left\langle j_{T}^{2}\right\rangle}\) and \(\left\langle|k_{Ty}|\right\rangle\) characterizing the jet properties. In the case of the trigger particle and the associated particles originating from the same jet, the width of near-side correlation distribution can be related as:

\[\sigma^{2}=\left\langle\Delta\phi^{2}\right\rangle=\left\langle\left(\frac{j_{ Ty}}{p_{Tassoc}}\right)^{2}+\left(\frac{j_{Ty}}{p_{Ttrig}}\right)^{2}\right\rangle \tag{4.4}\]

where we assume \(\left\langle j_{Ty}^{2}\right\rangle\ll p_{Ttrig}^{2}\) and \(p_{Tassoc}^{2}\).

Subsequently \(\sqrt{\left\langle j_{T}^{2}\right\rangle}\) can be expressed in the form [13]:

\[\sqrt{\left\langle j_{T}^{2}\right\rangle}=\sqrt{2\left\langle j_{Ty}^{2} \right\rangle}\simeq\sqrt{2}\frac{p_{Ttrig}p_{Tassoc}}{\sqrt{p_{Ttrig}^{2}+p_{ Tassoc}^{2}}}\sigma_{N} \tag{4.5}\]

where \(\sigma_{N}\) is the near-side correlation width. Figure 4.21-22 show dependence of the \(\sqrt{\left\langle j_{T}^{2}\right\rangle}\) with \(p_{Tassoc}\) for several regions of trigger particle \(p_{Ttrig}\), calculated according to (4.5) using the respecive widths from Gaussian fit to the correlation function (see figures 4.9, 4.11). As we can see in the data, \(\sqrt{\left\langle j_{T}^{2}\right\rangle}\) shows increase with \(p_{Tassoc}\) and saturation at a mean value \(\approx\) 600 MeV/c for \(p_{Tassoc}\)\(<\)1, 5\(>\) GeV/c. Calculated values for all biases together of \(\sqrt{\left\langle j_{T}^{2}\right\rangle}\) for d+Au collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{NN}}\) = 200 GeV are shown in the Table 4.3. These values are for \(p_{Ttrig}\) (3, 15) GeV/c and for \(p_{Tassoc}\) from interval \(1<p_{Tassoc}<p_{Ttrig}\).

\begin{tabular}{|c||c|c|} \hline  & \(\sqrt{\left\langle j_{T}^{2}\right\rangle}\) (track-track) & \(\sqrt{\left\langle j_{T}^{2}\right\rangle}\) (tower-track) \\ \hline \hline d+Au & 631 \(\pm\) 55 MeV/c & 579 \(\pm\) 62 MeV/c \\ \hline \end{tabular}

**Table 4.3:**\(\sqrt{\left\langle j_{T}^{2}\right\rangle}\) values for d+Au.

