#### 4.3.5 \(k_{t}\) measurements

All quantities needed for calculating the magnitude of \(k_{T}\) can be directly extracted from the correlation function, except for \(\left\langle z_{trig}\right\rangle\). For two particles with average transverse momenta \(\left\langle p_{Trig}\right\rangle\) and \(\left\langle p_{Tassoc}\right\rangle\) from the same jet, the width of the near-side peak (\(\sigma_{N}\)), can be \(\left\langle\left|j_{Ty}\right|\right\rangle\) defined as:

\[\left\langle\left|j_{Ty}\right|\right\rangle\approx\sqrt{\frac{2}{\pi}}\frac{ \left\langle p_{Trig}\right\rangle\left\langle p_{Tassoc}\right\rangle}{ \sqrt{\left\langle p_{Trig}\right\rangle^{2}+\left\langle p_{Tassoc}\right\rangle ^{2}}}\sigma_{N} \tag{4.6}\]

where \(\left\langle\left|j_{Ty}\right|\right\rangle\ll\left\langle p_{Trig}\right\rangle\) and \(\left\langle\left|j_{Ty}\right|\right\rangle\ll\left\langle p_{Tassoc}\right\rangle\). Thereafter we can determine \(\left\langle\left|k_{Ty}\right|\right\rangle\) using formula (6).

\[\left\langle\left|k_{Ty}\right|\right\rangle\left\langle z_{trig}\right\rangle= \frac{1}{x_{h}\sqrt{2}}\sqrt{\left\langle p_{Tassoc}\right\rangle^{2}sin^{2} \sqrt{\frac{2}{\pi}}\sigma_{A}-(1+x_{h})^{2}\left\langle\left|j_{Ty}\right| \right\rangle^{2}} \tag{4.7}\]

where \(x_{h}=\left\langle p_{Trig}\right\rangle/\left\langle p_{Tassoc}\right\rangle\) and \(\sigma_{A}\) is the width of the away-side peak [14]. Figures 4.23-24 show dependence of the \(\left\langle\left|k_{Ty}\right|\right\rangle\left\langle z_{trig}\right\rangle\) with \(p_{Tassoc}\) for several regions of trigger particle \(p_{Trig}\), calculated according to (4.7) using the respecive widths from Gaussian fit to the correlation function (see figures 4.10, 4.12).

To extract the magnitude of \(\left\langle\left|k_{Ty}\right|\right\rangle\) we need the external knowledge of the \(\left\langle z_{trig}\right\rangle=\left\langle p_{Trig}/p_{Tjet}\right\rangle\). In d+Au collision at \(\sqrt{s_{NN}}=200\) GeV is the value of \(\left\langle z_{trig}\right\rangle\simeq 0.85\)[14]. Calculated values of \(\left\langle\left|k_{Ty}\right|\right\rangle\left\langle z_{trig}\right\rangle\) for all bias together for d+Au collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{NN}}=200\) GeV are shown in the Table 4.4. These values are for \(p_{Trig}\)\(\left\langle 3\right\), 15) GeV/c and for \(p_{Tassoc}\) from interval \(1<p_{Tassoc}<p_{Trig}\).

